 class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 1951 to 2025, and on the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 43 of 75 years. In 2025 that middle ran 29% of normal in October to November and 17% in November to December. So far in 2026 it went the other way, with April to May at 176% of normal. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, and grid 10624 bottomed out at 29% that year.</p>"}
